WEBVTT

00:03.320 --> 00:04.670
Princess!

00:04.290 --> 00:05.530
Princess!

00:04.890 --> 00:06.450
Your Highness!

00:14.400 --> 00:16.650
Allow her to go.

00:19.450 --> 00:22.880
Shouldn't you have spoken to her?

00:23.730 --> 00:26.070
She'll probably come back soon enough.

00:27.300 --> 00:29.450
Ah, yes.

00:29.760 --> 00:33.470
The princess will discover a new world.

00:34.590 --> 00:36.570
<i>A new world...</i>

02:23.010 --> 02:25.000
They're so young, too.

02:23.080 --> 02:28.000
<b>Episode 1
<u>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h</u>

<b>Crunch Time with the Princess</b></b>

02:25.000 --> 02:27.460
I feel sorry for Machi-chan and her family.

02:27.460 --> 02:29.190
What are they going to do?

02:29.710 --> 02:30.930
Ichiro.

02:31.560 --> 02:33.530
What'll happen to us now?

02:33.530 --> 02:34.710
Don't worry.

02:35.700 --> 02:38.980
I'll take care of everything, somehow.

02:49.730 --> 02:51.440
rough sketches by 10AM!

02:51.970 --> 02:52.930
Oh, no!

03:01.730 --> 03:03.440
You got that, Machi-chan?

03:03.440 --> 03:04.450
Yep.

03:04.450 --> 03:07.450
The food Ichiro makes is easy to prepare.

03:12.480 --> 03:13.960
Thank you.

03:14.370 --> 03:15.980
You're welcome.

03:17.010 --> 03:19.470
Is Ichiro-kun busy again?

03:19.470 --> 03:21.890
There's a deadline coming.

03:23.740 --> 03:26.720
Ichiro, here's breakfast.

03:26.720 --> 03:28.210
Man, oh man!

03:29.770 --> 03:31.220
You okay?

03:31.220 --> 03:33.360
I-I-I'm fine.

03:34.970 --> 03:36.830
You must've overslept.

03:36.830 --> 03:38.860
You still haven't found an assistant?

03:39.190 --> 03:40.240
Right.

03:40.970 --> 03:44.600
It's hard to find anyone who'll 
do the finishing touches by hand.

03:44.600 --> 03:48.800
And Sano-kun and Akita-kun both 
suddenly did the solo debut thing.

03:50.270 --> 03:53.570
<i>My deadline's 7:00 the day after tomorrow.</i>

03:53.570 --> 03:57.030
<i>After rough sketches, 
I've got ten more pages to ink.</i>

03:57.030 --> 03:59.380
<i>For backgrounds... I've got zilch.</i>

04:01.160 --> 04:03.680
Don't worry! I'll be sure to get it done!

04:03.680 --> 04:07.630
And then, with the pay, 
we'll all go out for steak!

04:07.630 --> 04:10.340
Steak? Come on, Ichiro.

04:10.340 --> 04:12.010
Don't overextend yourself.

04:14.790 --> 04:19.190
<i>After I graduated high school and debuted 
as a manga artist, our father passed away.</i>

04:20.030 --> 04:23.790
<i>I was already serialized in a magazine, 
so instead of finding a job,</i>

04:23.790 --> 04:29.040
<i>I began living off manuscript fees and the
rent from the apartment building I inherited.</i>

04:29.030 --> 04:31.910
Alice and the Knight of Thorns
<b>Momo-Tea Kokone</b>

04:29.410 --> 04:31.900
<i>My stuff doesn't sell well, to be honest.</i>

04:32.200 --> 04:37.320
<i>But I've got to work hard to send 
my sister and brother to college.</i>

04:39.040 --> 04:40.290
Masahiro Morikuni

04:42.090 --> 04:43.800
Hello, Kuga speaking.

04:43.800 --> 04:45.310
It's Morikuni.

04:46.460 --> 04:47.800
You found an assistant?!

04:50.200 --> 04:51.340
Understood!

04:55.190 --> 04:57.640
I'll predict your future!

05:04.540 --> 05:06.110
See you later!

05:06.110 --> 05:07.530
Later.

05:07.530 --> 05:10.530
Wait! Tell me my fortune!

05:10.790 --> 05:12.230
What was his fortune?

05:14.580 --> 05:16.540
It came up colorless.

05:17.670 --> 05:20.800
Both his future and his 
manuscript are blank! Get it?

05:21.090 --> 05:22.400
Right...

05:24.050 --> 05:26.220
I'd better get going!

05:32.900 --> 05:35.880
They were traced, but her 
backgrounds are pretty good!

05:35.880 --> 05:38.210
<i>Seriously? That'd be great!</i>

05:38.210 --> 05:41.830
I only just saw it via email, 
so no guarantees.

05:40.440 --> 05:45.440
Accepting 
New Students

05:40.440 --> 05:45.440
<b>Dance</b>

05:40.440 --> 05:45.440
<b>Ballet</b>

05:41.830 --> 05:44.920
<i>Hey, I'm just thankful you got one at all!</i>

05:45.820 --> 05:49.230
Go and meet up with her. 
Seems she doesn't know the area.

05:49.230 --> 05:50.300
<i>Will do.</i>

05:51.350 --> 05:53.260
<i>At this point, I'd go any distance.</i>

06:04.500 --> 06:05.840
Excuse me.

06:15.590 --> 06:18.100
Um, are you the assistant?

06:20.820 --> 06:23.120
Are you Momo-Tea Kokone-sensei?

06:26.250 --> 06:29.710
Please call me by my real name,
 not my pen name!

06:29.710 --> 06:31.140
It's Ichiro Kuga.

06:33.340 --> 06:35.100
<i>If word gets around that it's me,</i>

06:35.100 --> 06:37.770
<i>it might end up being embarrassing 
for Machi and Fumio.</i>

06:37.770 --> 06:40.620
Your brother draws manga?

06:40.620 --> 06:42.990
Is he famous? Get us his autograph!

06:42.990 --> 06:43.890
Shut up.

06:44.140 --> 06:45.900
I beg your pardon.

06:45.900 --> 06:49.960
I am Shiori Goshiki, 
and I hope to be your assistant.

06:49.960 --> 06:51.750
It's nice to meet you.

06:52.390 --> 06:53.680
Likewise.

06:53.680 --> 06:56.710
W-Would you mind if we got right to work?

06:57.830 --> 06:58.790
All right.

07:01.520 --> 07:03.760
<b>Hiiragi Apartments</b>

07:09.840 --> 07:11.380
I apologize.

07:11.380 --> 07:14.430
I would have liked to give you 
a day to get used to things.

07:14.430 --> 07:17.390
But we're in a rush today,
 so we need to get to work.

07:17.390 --> 07:18.290
Okay.

07:18.580 --> 07:23.560
You can use the art tools here 
or ones you're already used to.

07:23.560 --> 07:26.600
Here are the storyboards 
and some past works.

07:26.600 --> 07:27.920
All right.

07:29.940 --> 07:31.200
Um...

07:32.440 --> 07:35.680
There's a room where assistants can 
change their clothes, if needed.

07:37.370 --> 07:40.570
That's okay. I always dress like this.

07:40.820 --> 07:42.170
Well...

07:48.910 --> 07:49.750
Here.

07:50.210 --> 07:53.200
Please borrow this, 
since your clothes look expensive.

07:53.200 --> 07:54.730
Is that so?

07:54.730 --> 07:58.630
Don't worry if it gets dirty.

08:02.660 --> 08:06.720
Okay, please start by doing panel 
borders and backgrounds for these.

08:06.720 --> 08:07.620
Will do.

08:11.840 --> 08:14.670
<i>Sh-She's fast! And skillful!</i>

08:14.670 --> 08:17.830
<i>And also, very beautiful.</i>

08:18.850 --> 08:21.520
Your line work is beautiful!

08:21.520 --> 08:23.320
Have you been an assistant for long?

08:23.320 --> 08:25.740
No, this is my first time.

08:25.740 --> 08:27.720
For real?!

08:28.000 --> 08:31.740
I learned using this book, 
<i>Shojo Manga Lessons</i>.

08:32.120 --> 08:34.160
That book's pretty old.

08:35.730 --> 08:39.970
Oh, but it was compiled by 
Funeko Horehoro-sensei.

08:39.970 --> 08:41.180
Not bad.

08:41.180 --> 08:42.100
Excuse me.

08:42.740 --> 08:44.130
What should I do next?

08:44.130 --> 08:45.620
Oh, sorry.

08:46.710 --> 08:47.380
Let's see.

08:48.030 --> 08:49.800
Ink the highlights on this hair.

08:49.800 --> 08:50.870
All right.

08:52.380 --> 08:53.860
I'm done.

08:53.860 --> 08:54.620
Okay.

08:55.230 --> 08:57.580
Would you mind scraping this screentone?

08:57.580 --> 08:58.260
Sure.

09:01.380 --> 09:02.680
Finished.

09:03.210 --> 09:04.010
What's next?

09:06.130 --> 09:10.910
<i>I'm </i>so<i> grateful! I'll </i>definitely<i> 
make the deadline now!</i>

09:10.910 --> 09:12.400
Um...

09:13.020 --> 09:14.260
It's flawless!

09:14.770 --> 09:16.500
We're home!

09:16.500 --> 09:17.630
Home.

09:23.020 --> 09:24.410
Welcome back.

09:26.450 --> 09:29.280
Are you a gemstone princess?!

09:29.740 --> 09:32.800
No, children, not gemstone.

09:32.800 --> 09:34.240
Machi.

09:34.240 --> 09:38.040
This is Shiori Goshiki-san, 
who became my assistant in a hurry.

09:38.040 --> 09:39.670
Welcome.

09:39.670 --> 09:42.160
Wait, have you been working her non-stop?

09:42.160 --> 09:44.550
Taking breaks improves efficiency!

09:44.550 --> 09:46.550
I-I'm sorry.

09:46.950 --> 09:49.300
Does she know where to
 find the sink and bathroom?

09:49.300 --> 09:51.330
Oh, that's <i>right!</i>

09:51.330 --> 09:53.240
Don't forget these things!

09:54.010 --> 09:55.470
Ten-minute break!

09:55.970 --> 09:58.280
I'll show you around!

09:58.280 --> 09:59.550
Please do.

10:00.410 --> 10:02.700
Each of these has a bedroom, 
dining area, and kitchenette.

10:03.350 --> 10:06.110
You're guaranteed privacy,
 and there's also a common area.

10:06.110 --> 10:08.160
They're "social apartments."

10:08.160 --> 10:10.080
Social apartments?

10:10.580 --> 10:14.470
All sorts of people live in them: 
a manicurist, an office worker, etc.

10:14.470 --> 10:17.080
Also our cousin, Chibi-chan.

10:17.080 --> 10:18.530
Chibi-chan?

10:19.340 --> 10:23.310
Ichiro is a live-in landlord
 and manga artist!

10:23.310 --> 10:24.630
Now I see.

10:25.350 --> 10:27.990
This is the communal kitchen and lounge.

10:28.220 --> 10:31.700
There's an oven, so those who 
want to cook use this it a lot.

10:32.570 --> 10:36.710
The rooms besides ours only have showers, 
but there's a public bath nearby.

10:37.140 --> 10:38.870
That's good to know.

10:39.180 --> 10:43.360
So, this is the vacant room that 
assistants use for staying overnight.

10:43.950 --> 10:45.530
It's lovely.

10:46.010 --> 10:47.440
You'll use it, right?

10:50.890 --> 10:52.680
Food's here!

10:56.360 --> 10:58.250
Huh? Where's Goshiki-san?

10:59.090 --> 11:01.750
She said she'd eat alone 
in the assistant's room.

11:03.250 --> 11:06.260
<i>Maybe I should have told 
her to go out to eat.</i>

11:06.520 --> 11:07.910
Maybe...

11:07.910 --> 11:09.890
She has a mouth on the back of her head!

11:10.320 --> 11:12.650
Or she's an animal spirit 
who's repaying you.

11:12.650 --> 11:14.830
Don't be weird about it.

11:14.830 --> 11:17.630
You know what she is? She's pro-level.

11:17.630 --> 11:19.340
No, goddess-level!

11:19.650 --> 11:20.930
Okay!

11:20.930 --> 11:22.950
I sure hope she stays on.

11:22.950 --> 11:24.160
Stays on.

11:37.580 --> 11:39.110
Think I'll make some tea.

11:39.110 --> 11:40.640
I'll do it.

11:40.640 --> 11:41.790
No, that's okay.

11:42.130 --> 11:44.610
I just finished this work I was doing.

11:49.210 --> 11:50.520
Huh?

11:51.310 --> 11:53.270
You knew where the tea was?

11:53.270 --> 11:55.510
Yes. Would you like some?

11:55.510 --> 11:57.020
Uh-uh.

11:57.020 --> 11:59.310
We'd just have to go to the bathroom again.

11:59.640 --> 12:03.830
Why don't you stop for the day? 
We don't wanna turn into a sweatshop.

12:05.030 --> 12:06.620
I can keep going.

12:07.040 --> 12:10.700
Actually, I thought I'd get 
even fewer breaks than this.

12:11.140 --> 12:12.830
I heard it's a tight schedule.

12:12.830 --> 12:14.730
Oh, yeah.

12:15.270 --> 12:18.710
Ichiro's no good at asking 
for help, even with work.

12:18.710 --> 12:22.650
He said he's saving up money 
so he can send us to college.

12:23.940 --> 12:28.590
He says he has to be like a parent to us.

12:29.430 --> 12:32.190
And he tries to take care 
of everything by himself.

12:34.690 --> 12:39.970
Even without connection, you guys have 
some great communication going on.

12:39.970 --> 12:40.860
Commu...

12:41.260 --> 12:42.220
What?

12:46.090 --> 12:48.620
Well, anyway, get some sleep.

12:49.080 --> 12:50.030
Okay.

12:59.210 --> 13:00.490
So cute.

13:02.460 --> 13:03.520
Here.

13:04.270 --> 13:07.820
Thank you. Go ahead and stop for the day.

13:11.660 --> 13:13.490
Just these panel borders.

13:13.970 --> 13:17.850
Thanks, I appreciate it.

13:18.480 --> 13:21.270
Want the radio on to keep you awake?

13:21.270 --> 13:22.590
No, thank you.

13:22.590 --> 13:26.280
I know. Why don't I tell you about myself?

13:26.280 --> 13:27.410
Sure.

13:30.350 --> 13:35.790
I'm nearly 19, and before this year, 
I had never read any manga.

13:35.790 --> 13:38.330
Wow, that's unusual.

13:38.840 --> 13:42.420
Well, not unheard of. 
Your parents didn't let you?

13:43.450 --> 13:44.800
That's correct.

13:45.970 --> 13:49.060
It's just that my grandmother loved books,

13:49.060 --> 13:51.440
and she let me alone see her collection.

13:51.430 --> 13:54.180
Alice and the
 Knight of Thorns

13:51.430 --> 13:54.180
<b>Momo-Tea Kokone</b>

13:51.940 --> 13:54.180
Your manga was part of it.

13:54.460 --> 13:55.350
Huh?!

13:55.350 --> 13:56.670
I was surprised.

13:57.360 --> 13:59.680
<i>Did I draw something weird?</i>

14:00.050 --> 14:04.200
I never realized such 
flights of fancy existed.

14:04.630 --> 14:06.200
<i>That's not a compliment.</i>

14:06.550 --> 14:08.930
A misunderstanding leads to a quarrel.

14:08.930 --> 14:13.430
But a mysterious fever called love 
somehow grows out of it all.

14:14.280 --> 14:18.700
There are so many such stories, 
ever in different forms.

14:19.610 --> 14:22.840
Yeah, that's shojo manga for you.

14:22.840 --> 14:27.210
Constant ups and downs. 
From one problem to the next.

14:28.010 --> 14:32.230
But I found all that 
discomfort to be touching.

14:33.300 --> 14:35.520
Hey, Goshiki-san...

14:35.520 --> 14:39.260
Usually, the workload is a little 
more evenly paced around here.

14:39.800 --> 14:41.730
So can I continue to count on you?

14:42.320 --> 14:43.220
Yes!

15:05.310 --> 15:06.380
Could you...

15:07.600 --> 15:09.630
Hair highlights, right?

15:09.630 --> 15:10.500
Yeah.

15:16.510 --> 15:18.380
The day's already gone by?!

15:19.340 --> 15:22.640
Thanks, Goshiki-san. 
This is enough for today.

15:23.730 --> 15:25.530
I can keep going.

15:25.830 --> 15:27.120
Thank you.

15:27.730 --> 15:31.080
But once this page is done,
 that just leaves finishing touches.

15:31.080 --> 15:32.400
I can do those myself.

15:33.540 --> 15:35.400
I'm reluctant to stop.

15:35.800 --> 15:38.230
If you push too hard, you'll burn out.

15:38.730 --> 15:44.740
Let's see, the finished manuscript 
is... one page, two...

15:49.330 --> 15:50.420
What's the matter?

15:51.270 --> 15:53.920
It's missing... one.

15:53.920 --> 15:56.010
Missing one?

15:57.510 --> 15:59.440
Hold on! Hold on!

15:59.440 --> 16:02.050
Um, what do you mean the 
manuscript's missing one?

16:00.180 --> 16:02.050
Don't tell me...

16:02.380 --> 16:06.070
No, it's here! I think 
I remember drawing it!

16:06.070 --> 16:07.530
Found it!

16:14.170 --> 16:16.420
<i>I barely even touched it!</i>

16:16.750 --> 16:18.250
Blenk.

16:20.630 --> 16:22.750
I can keep going.

16:22.750 --> 16:25.680
No, it's okay! I'll figure something out.

16:25.960 --> 16:30.170
<i>Rough sketch, inking, finishes. 
That'll take 2-3 hours.</i>

16:30.170 --> 16:32.140
<i>Maybe I </i>should<i> ask Goshiki-san to...</i>

16:32.140 --> 16:36.860
<i>No, an all-nighter is too much to 
ask when she's not permanent yet.</i>

16:38.450 --> 16:40.400
<i>I'll finish just in time, if I don't sleep.</i>

16:40.670 --> 16:44.920
I am unable to guess your feelings.

16:46.250 --> 16:50.180
If you really do want help, 
please tell me honestly.

16:53.160 --> 16:55.110
Do you need assistance?

16:56.330 --> 16:58.240
<i>I just can't afford to miss the deadline.</i>

16:59.020 --> 17:01.140
<i>I'd lose a month's worth of manuscript pay.</i>

17:02.120 --> 17:04.920
<i>I know I'm your mother, 
but I have a new life now.</i>

17:06.000 --> 17:09.630
<i>Worst case, I could submit 
it with just inks and fills.</i>

17:09.630 --> 17:12.550
<i>This one page could have some 
white space left in it.</i>

17:13.090 --> 17:15.420
Work hard at the manga, Ichiro.

17:15.860 --> 17:18.670
<i>If I just do the best I can do...</i>

17:19.870 --> 17:21.130
Do you...

17:22.940 --> 17:24.560
need assistance?

17:27.580 --> 17:29.840
I'm sorry, Goshiki-san!

17:29.840 --> 17:32.060
I don't really want to cut corners!

17:32.580 --> 17:34.330
Please work with me all night!

17:35.570 --> 17:37.310
I'll give you overtime pay!

17:39.270 --> 17:40.570
I will work with you.

17:51.020 --> 17:53.610
F-Finished!

17:56.160 --> 18:01.230
I'll make copies, send an email, 
and check it over.

18:02.020 --> 18:04.030
You sleep, Gohiki-han...

18:04.660 --> 18:05.850
Right.

18:11.660 --> 18:13.990
<i>I'm so tired.</i>

18:13.990 --> 18:16.530
<i>I've kept such regular hours lately.</i>

18:16.530 --> 18:21.220
<i>I haven't... done an all-nighter... in ages.</i>

18:26.100 --> 18:28.060
Shoot, I fell asleep briefly.

18:30.230 --> 18:34.400
And Goshiki-san didn't get far, either.

18:34.950 --> 18:35.690
Huh?!

18:38.190 --> 18:40.010
<i>There's a G-pen sticking her!</i>

18:41.380 --> 18:42.350
Look out!

18:46.550 --> 18:49.240
<i>O-Outer space?</i>

19:01.910 --> 19:05.940
Now you and my stinger have been linked.

19:08.220 --> 19:13.140
That amounts to the two of us vowing 
to bind our destinies together!

19:14.640 --> 19:18.040
I just had some kind of hallucination.

19:19.770 --> 19:21.540
I'm saying that in my land,

19:21.540 --> 19:25.720
it's an act permitted only to 
those in a marital relationship.

19:25.720 --> 19:27.350
Marital?

19:27.350 --> 19:31.730
I never thought you were the type to touch 
someone's body while they're asleep!

19:31.730 --> 19:34.730
W-Wait, you've got the wrong idea!

19:34.730 --> 19:38.360
I thought, well, there was a 
sharp object stuck in you!

19:38.800 --> 19:39.980
Sharp object?

19:43.920 --> 19:45.490
This is how it looked!

19:48.290 --> 19:50.450
You were trying to save my life?

19:50.810 --> 19:52.740
Yeah, and I messed up!

19:52.740 --> 19:54.630
I mean, sorry.

19:54.630 --> 19:58.470
If I hadn't been half asleep, 
I might not have mistaken it.

20:00.280 --> 20:04.110
Goshiki-san, I realize I'm the one who 
asked you to pull an all-nighter.

20:04.760 --> 20:05.960
I'm sorry.

20:06.940 --> 20:08.810
I'm sorry, too.

20:09.410 --> 20:13.850
If it looked like a sharp object 
was sticking me, then thank you.

20:14.280 --> 20:16.320
<i>That stinger thing.</i>

20:17.010 --> 20:19.090
<i>It was like a tail.</i>

20:19.600 --> 20:21.510
<i>Are there people with tails?</i>

20:22.170 --> 20:26.070
<i>No, if that's the case, 
asking about it might be rude.</i>

20:27.100 --> 20:31.510
You and I only just met,
 and you don't know anything.

20:32.190 --> 20:36.200
Maybe it was lucky that you 
happened to touch me this way?

20:36.630 --> 20:40.790
We only just met, but I already 
know that you're reliable,

20:40.790 --> 20:43.510
and you do meticulous work.

20:43.930 --> 20:46.350
That's why I feel really sorry.

20:46.350 --> 20:49.780
I would say I feel awkward.

20:49.780 --> 20:51.640
Not lucky.

20:53.420 --> 20:55.750
Then, sure enough.

20:55.750 --> 21:00.710
Physical contact must be wonderful 
between those who trust one another.

21:00.710 --> 21:02.330
Like in the stories.

21:04.400 --> 21:06.650
Just who are you, Goshiki-san?

21:07.130 --> 21:10.230
I am the princess of the Star People.

21:10.230 --> 21:11.030
Huh?!

21:11.440 --> 21:14.060
I don't desire marriage born of mishap.

21:14.060 --> 21:17.550
I figure that love should come first.

21:18.400 --> 21:20.730
No, wait a minute!

21:20.730 --> 21:23.920
You shouldn't joke like that with 
a coworker you don't know well!

21:23.920 --> 21:28.050
I'm raising young kids. I can't 
have weird rumors going around!

21:29.210 --> 21:32.050
I wouldn't say I don't know you well.

21:33.940 --> 21:37.820
I thought your art was the 
simplest in that magazine,

21:37.820 --> 21:40.280
so as practice, I started out by copying it.

21:40.980 --> 21:46.710
The more I traced, the more I could tell how 
much time and care was spent creating it.

21:47.290 --> 21:52.450
That's why I would say 
I know you by your work.

21:52.760 --> 21:55.820
I suppose you could say I'm your fan?

21:56.230 --> 21:59.840
Well, in a way that makes it even worse.

22:00.430 --> 22:02.460
Oh, right.

22:02.460 --> 22:05.330
We'll start as friends, then.

22:07.340 --> 22:09.460
Here's hoping for the best.

22:10.120 --> 22:12.460
Y-Yeah...

23:46.810 --> 23:49.070
I'm glad such a great person has come!

23:49.070 --> 23:50.840
He said she's "goddess level"!

23:50.840 --> 23:52.890
They've gone somewhere together.

23:52.890 --> 23:53.820
The heat is on!

23:53.820 --> 23:55.480
He's burning up.

23:55.480 --> 23:56.460
Why?!

23:55.950 --> 23:59.950
<b>Episode 2</b>

23:55.950 --> 23:59.950
<b>Shopping with the Princess</b>

23:56.460 --> 23:57.530
Ouch, hot.
